1
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:43,334
Fuck!

2
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:54,405
Fuck, I'm already hungry again.

3
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:58,368
The meal was expensive as hell too.

4
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:47,417
MOUSETRAP

5
00:02:57,927 --> 00:03:00,430
Shouldn't we have gone back to that place?

6
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:02,265
He was there.

7
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:04,642
As if he'd still be there. Fuck.

8
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:07,854
Besides, those hit men?
They were after me.

9
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:08,980
Who were they?

10
00:03:09,063 --> 00:03:10,356
None of your business, punk.

11
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:13,109
Shit. This is getting out of fucking hand.

12
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:15,737
But how the hell did he know
where we were?

13
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:17,447
He knew we were at the motel too.

14
00:03:17,947 --> 00:03:19,532
I even threw away my phone.

15
00:03:20,116 --> 00:03:21,409
Who knows?

16
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:23,703
Maybe he's tailing us.

17
00:03:27,498 --> 00:03:29,500
Fuck! Every time I get involved with you,

18
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:31,920
my life goes to total shit!

19
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:35,715
Once I get my fucking money back,
don't ever come near me. Got it?

20
00:03:38,718 --> 00:03:40,762
Hey, fuck, which island is it?

21
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,268
That bastard will be there for sure.

22
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:49,062
At least a trace of him.

23
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:56,402
They were brought in on a restaurant call?

24
00:03:56,486 --> 00:03:58,780
Both unidentified persons?

25
00:03:58,863 --> 00:04:00,406
Yes, that's right.

26
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:01,407
Oh man.

27
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:04,535
What's this world fucking coming to?

28
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:08,539
Jesus, his jaw's totally smashed.

29
00:04:09,207 --> 00:04:10,917
I know how that feels.

30
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:11,876
Hey!

31
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,796
The nurses say you speak some Korean.

32
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:17,423
That bastard's not talking. You talk.

33
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:21,844
Why are you both unidentified persons?
How do you end up like that, huh?

34
00:04:23,721 --> 00:04:24,681
Are you sleeping?

35
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:27,433
This bastard's eyelids are twitching.

36
00:04:31,145 --> 00:04:33,189
Hey, where's Noja?

37
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:35,942
Just tell me, and I'll leave you alone.

38
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:43,533
You got into an argument
in the parking lot.

39
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:46,911
And then he just started
beating the shit out of you.

40
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:49,914
So you guys are basically just victims.

41
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:50,915
Right?

42
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:52,959
Damn, you must be so upset.

43
00:04:56,212 --> 00:04:58,589
Is that how you want it in the report?

44
00:05:20,903 --> 00:05:22,655
What the hell is going on?

45
00:05:24,073 --> 00:05:26,326
Whatever the hell is going on,

46
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:28,536
why are we handling this?

47
00:05:28,619 --> 00:05:29,787
Why not Violent Crimes?

48
00:05:29,871 --> 00:05:32,498
We've got a shit ton of work
to do already.

49
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:34,917
Man, what a headache.

50
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:36,836
That tip's killing us.

51
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:39,130
Find this guy first.

52
00:05:39,213 --> 00:05:40,965
He runs an identity fraud ring.

53
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:47,305
Catch him and lean on him.
You're probably looking at a promotion.

54
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:56,356
What are you doing? Aren't you gonna go?

55
00:05:57,357 --> 00:05:58,775
Hurry up. Go get him.

56
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:01,319
You think you're in charge?

57
00:06:01,402 --> 00:06:04,322
No one's in charge here.
We're all just fucking grunts.

58
00:06:05,531 --> 00:06:06,532
Where are you going?

59
00:06:07,158 --> 00:06:08,785
I'm going to work.

60
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:10,453
That little…

61
00:06:12,955 --> 00:06:14,123
Come on, sir.

62
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:15,958
Why not send him to Violent Crimes?

63
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:18,086
He freaking loves those cases.

64
00:06:18,586 --> 00:06:20,880
It's you who's got
the Violent Crimes look.

65
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:23,091
Damn it.

66
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:32,767
Come on. Let's go!

67
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:36,062
Hey.

68
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:41,526
Can't a cop enjoy his fucking hobby
on his day off? Huh?

69
00:06:41,609 --> 00:06:43,694
This place isn't illegal!

70
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:46,697
Huh? What's with your face?

71
00:06:47,365 --> 00:06:49,992
Is this place illegal?

72
00:06:50,868 --> 00:06:52,829
Hey. Go get the owner.

73
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:54,997
What's the owner's name?

74
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:58,000
I said go get the owner!

75
00:06:58,084 --> 00:07:01,462
Yes, I'm Kang Myeong-su.
What seems to be the problem?

76
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:06,509
- Kang Myeong-su?
- Yes.

77
00:07:08,636 --> 00:07:10,138
Kang Myeong-su?

78
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:14,892
You look familiar,
but the name doesn't ring a bell.

79
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:16,394
Have we met?

80
00:07:18,479 --> 00:07:19,605
I don't think so.

81
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:20,815
Really?

82
00:07:23,025 --> 00:07:24,110
So,

83
00:07:24,735 --> 00:07:27,029
you don't have Go-Stop here?

84
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:30,450
Well, what do you want?

85
00:07:30,533 --> 00:07:31,909
Right.

86
00:07:39,792 --> 00:07:42,420
We could come by every day. Okay?

87
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:46,507
We've got all the fucking time
in the world. Okay?

88
00:08:03,566 --> 00:08:05,359
Doesn't look like he'll last the week.

89
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:07,570
- Terminal liver cancer?
- Yes, sir.

90
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:10,031
- Where did you find him?
- A homeless shelter.

91
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:11,782
I laundered his identity clean.

92
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:18,706
He was born in Korea,

93
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:21,626
and now he's dying as an illegal alien.

94
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:27,215
Hey, Myeong-su.

95
00:08:27,298 --> 00:08:28,883
Hey, the cops were just here.

96
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:30,051
Yeah?

97
00:08:30,551 --> 00:08:32,053
That's nothing new.

98
00:08:32,136 --> 00:08:34,013
<i>They won't get a warrant. No evidence.</i>

99
00:08:34,096 --> 00:08:35,431
They were looking for you.

100
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:36,891
<i>Don't come here.</i>

101
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:38,184
I'll handle it somehow.

102
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:40,561
Noja, that son of a bitch.

103
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:42,897
He's gonna fuck us all up.

104
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:46,817
Why the hell did you send those morons?
Now it's a bigger mess!

105
00:08:46,901 --> 00:08:49,237
You couldn't find someone
who could do it right?

106
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:52,031
For fuck's sake. Forget it! I'll do it.

107
00:08:52,114 --> 00:08:53,866
You just handle the site, okay?

108
00:08:56,369 --> 00:08:58,371
This fucking bastard.

109
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:01,582
Seriously, this fucking bastard.

110
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:03,709
Man, this fucking dumbass.

111
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:06,462
He's so fucking useless. For fuck's sake.

112
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:11,551
A business trip?

113
00:09:11,634 --> 00:09:13,094
I'll go get him real quick.

114
00:09:16,013 --> 00:09:17,640
You told me to go start a fire.

115
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:19,475
I did, but he still hasn't come out.

116
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:22,186
He will if you keep it up.
Those two are in it together.

117
00:09:22,728 --> 00:09:25,147
Hey! You dumping the legwork on us?

118
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:27,900
Looks like that gut
could use some legwork, asshole.

119
00:09:29,318 --> 00:09:30,611
Take Chang-u or Min-ho.

120
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:32,071
I'm putting someone on you.

121
00:09:32,154 --> 00:09:34,115
I prefer working alone.

122
00:09:34,657 --> 00:09:37,201
Yeah. I prefer working alone too.

123
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:38,369
You can take them all.

124
00:09:38,452 --> 00:09:40,705
Come on, sir. I prefer working alone too.

125
00:09:40,788 --> 00:09:41,664
Damn it.

126
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:43,082
Hey, kid. Follow me.

127
00:09:43,165 --> 00:09:44,250
Why?

128
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:47,003
"Why?" Y comes after X, you bastard.

129
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:50,423
Look at him taking his sweet time.
He's just strolling.

130
00:09:50,506 --> 00:09:51,549
That bastard.

131
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:57,680
Where are we going?

132
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:02,560
- When was the last time you saw the ocean?
- What?

133
00:10:02,643 --> 00:10:04,645
The ocean, you bastard.

134
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:11,754
If this is his parents' restaurant,
that lady must be his mom.

135
00:11:11,837 --> 00:11:12,672
Right?

136
00:11:14,298 --> 00:11:15,841
Stay out of this. I'll handle it.

137
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:19,095
You look too…

138
00:11:29,146 --> 00:11:30,231
You're not?

139
00:11:30,314 --> 00:11:33,693
Oh, I'm just the new owner here.

140
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:38,531
I know the previous owner well.
We lived in the same neighborhood.

141
00:11:39,448 --> 00:11:43,577
Oh my, he went through a lot
because of that troublemaker son of his.

142
00:11:43,661 --> 00:11:46,622
I mean, he didn't even visit
when his father died.

143
00:11:47,206 --> 00:11:51,377
He only showed up briefly
when I was taking over the shop.

144
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,837
Just to collect the money.

145
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:55,381
So when was that…

146
00:11:56,716 --> 00:12:01,011
That was maybe three or four years ago.

147
00:12:02,263 --> 00:12:04,932
Oh, go to the harbor. His friend's there.

148
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:23,409
Hey!

149
00:12:26,495 --> 00:12:27,413
Hey!

150
00:12:28,664 --> 00:12:30,040
Do you know Seo Yu-min?

151
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:34,503
Yu-min?

152
00:12:34,587 --> 00:12:35,546
Yes.

153
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:40,634
What about that bastard?

154
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:43,512
Well, you see--

155
00:12:43,596 --> 00:12:44,513
Hey.

156
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:49,226
We're from Seoul.

157
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:57,860
Our squad leader may not sound like it,
but he really cares about you.

158
00:12:58,652 --> 00:13:00,696
Just tell him to worry about himself.

159
00:13:01,405 --> 00:13:02,782
You two go way back, right?

160
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:05,910
Yeah, all the way back
to when he was dating his wife.

161
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:09,079
That's about the same as us.

162
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:12,124
Hey.

163
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:15,461
He only turned out okay
because he met the right woman.

164
00:13:15,544 --> 00:13:17,213
That's why they're happy together.

165
00:13:17,296 --> 00:13:19,256
His wife deserves some credit,

166
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:21,091
but he also treats her really well.

167
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:22,092
Very affectionate.

168
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:25,137
Yeah. He doesn't break walls
like someone here.

169
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:27,515
He's not facing a divorce either, right?

170
00:13:28,307 --> 00:13:30,518
Why are we back on that again?

171
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:35,105
I'm just not cut out for family.

172
00:13:35,606 --> 00:13:37,358
I'm an orphan. Damn it.

173
00:13:37,441 --> 00:13:40,778
I don't even know
who my real parents are, you know?

174
00:13:40,861 --> 00:13:42,446
I was abandoned at an orphanage.

175
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:45,491
Well, I was adopted.

176
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:49,578
Fuck, I guess they didn't like me.
They sent me back.

177
00:13:50,162 --> 00:13:51,121
Huh?

178
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:54,250
Back to the orphanage.
Adopted again, sent back again.

179
00:13:55,459 --> 00:13:57,753
- Kid.
- Sir?

180
00:13:58,254 --> 00:14:00,589
I'm just not meant to have a family.

181
00:14:03,634 --> 00:14:04,593
We're your family.

182
00:14:05,761 --> 00:14:07,221
Bullshit.

183
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:12,893
Family, my ass. Once they turn away,
they're just strangers.

184
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:19,775
In the end, we all live like islands.

185
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:49,972
It's been a while. What a mess.

186
00:14:50,681 --> 00:14:52,099
This is Yu-min's place.

187
00:14:54,018 --> 00:14:56,437
Why are you looking for him?
Did he scam someone again?

188
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:59,356
Oh, so he scammed someone around here too?

189
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,859
He borrowed from everyone
and made a mess of things.

190
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:03,193
Money again?

191
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:05,321
Yeah, money. A lot of money.

192
00:15:05,404 --> 00:15:06,697
Figures.

193
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:08,616
He hasn't been here for a long time.

194
00:15:08,699 --> 00:15:10,034
It sat empty for a while.

195
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:12,494
Someone rented it
for a few months last year.

196
00:15:12,578 --> 00:15:15,873
He wasn't a fisherman.
I think he said he was a writer.

197
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:18,417
Actually, he looked kinda like you--

198
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,629
Well, I mean,
have you seen him since then?

199
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:23,756
No.

200
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:27,593
That bastard somehow
had a girl on his arm.

201
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:29,053
A girl?

202
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:31,305
Yeah, he showed up with some girl.

203
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:34,141
They stayed here together
when they came down.

204
00:16:53,303 --> 00:16:55,472
Goddamn it. What the hell are you doing?

205
00:17:00,436 --> 00:17:01,437
What about his friend?

206
00:17:02,062 --> 00:17:03,147
He left!

207
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:06,233
He doesn't have his number.
They haven't been in touch.

208
00:17:06,316 --> 00:17:07,317
So what now?

209
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:11,989
Apparently, he's got stuff in the attic.
We should check it out.

210
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:14,908
Weren't you fucking listening earlier?

211
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,703
Damn it.

212
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:26,962
Shit.

213
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:31,091
Hey, I think that bastard Yu-min
is the rat bastard.

214
00:17:31,592 --> 00:17:34,178
If those two bastards aren't the same guy,

215
00:17:34,678 --> 00:17:36,555
how do their movements all lead

216
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:40,100
to a house all the way out here?

217
00:17:50,819 --> 00:17:51,820
Hey, come here.

218
00:17:59,661 --> 00:18:01,371
Hey, this is the rat hole.

219
00:18:05,709 --> 00:18:07,211
Sheesh.

220
00:18:14,218 --> 00:18:16,637
<i>He said he'd been preparing</i>
<i>for a long time.</i>

221
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:19,098
<i>He even changed his face and voice</i>

222
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:21,642
<i>to take everything you've got.</i>

223
00:18:22,226 --> 00:18:23,727
<i>Didn't I tell you?</i>

224
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:26,730
<i>Everything was planned.</i>

225
00:18:28,023 --> 00:18:30,943
<i>The phone, the broken glass…</i>

226
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:34,905
<i>Maybe even Da-eun's kidnapping.</i>

227
00:19:27,124 --> 00:19:28,125
Hey, is this it?

228
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:29,877
Huh?

229
00:19:31,044 --> 00:19:33,088
The stuff he was keeping here.

230
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:37,801
Shit.

231
00:19:44,224 --> 00:19:45,475
What the hell?

232
00:19:46,059 --> 00:19:49,146
Who the hell parks this close to the edge?

233
00:19:49,229 --> 00:19:51,481
- I'm sorry.
- You trying to make me fall off?

234
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:56,320
Hey, who do we ask?

235
00:19:56,403 --> 00:19:57,487
Hold on a sec.

236
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:01,575
Oh.

237
00:20:02,075 --> 00:20:04,036
Excuse me. We're with the police.

238
00:20:04,536 --> 00:20:07,497
We're looking for someone.

239
00:20:13,003 --> 00:20:14,338
Hey, Jeong-bae!

240
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:16,924
Cops are here again.

241
00:20:21,678 --> 00:20:23,764
What does he mean by "again"?

242
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:27,935
Hello.

243
00:20:28,518 --> 00:20:29,853
Mr. Jeong-bae!

244
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:31,813
Are you Mr. Jeong-bae?

245
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:45,911
What are those pictures?

246
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:49,915
Good fucking times, huh?

247
00:20:56,171 --> 00:20:57,172
Wait.

248
00:20:58,465 --> 00:21:00,217
So this is that bastard Yu-min?

249
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:01,927
Yeah.

250
00:21:02,636 --> 00:21:04,596
Shit. Are you sure?

251
00:21:09,476 --> 00:21:11,353
We really are all tangled up.

252
00:21:12,771 --> 00:21:14,231
I know this bastard too.

253
00:21:14,314 --> 00:21:15,691
How do you know Yu-min?

254
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:32,249
You came?

255
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:35,168
Punk, you just got home after two days?

256
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:38,046
I've spent a month looking for you.

257
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:40,590
You borrowed money from a loan shark.

258
00:21:40,674 --> 00:21:43,969
Why does a kid like you
need money so badly?

259
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:46,471
Have you eaten?

260
00:21:49,308 --> 00:21:50,142
Sit.

261
00:21:50,642 --> 00:21:53,228
I made two <i>ramyeon</i>.
Let's eat before we go.

262
00:21:57,691 --> 00:21:58,525
Go where?

263
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:01,486
To the guy looking for you.

264
00:22:06,825 --> 00:22:08,285
You're not running away. Okay?

265
00:22:08,368 --> 00:22:10,912
It's cold out. Let's not make it harder.

266
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:13,832
I'm not running away.

267
00:22:15,292 --> 00:22:16,793
If I can't pay it back,

268
